WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.672
♪♪

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.674
We are here to celebrate

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.577
Selena Gomez, tonight

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.178
because of this really thoughtful

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.113
and courageous

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.180
and quite frankly

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.717
brilliant documentary film and
we are going to do it here at

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:21.988
the historic Apple Tower Theatre
in Downtown Los Angeles.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:26.493
And we are going to do it with
You and the fans and Selena

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:30.697
Please welcome, Selena Gomez.

00:00:45.672 --> 00:00:48.000
Thanks, guys.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.118
I love you.
it is a different kind of

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.888
Applause, I think, it feels
different. Don't you think?

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:59.261
I do. I think people have seen my
diary so I'm like.

00:00:59.261 --> 00:01:03.797
It is always so supportive,
like, we love you.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.433
It is great to see you.
This is cool, what a great

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.169
location for us to
Be able to hang out and talk.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.839
Thank you so much for being
here, this is beautiful.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:19.746
I wanted to start by asking
the most obvious human question

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.882
that we should start every
conversation with, which is, how

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:27.921
are you?
I do not know, actually.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:31.424
It has been weird.
The documentary exists and it is

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:36.062
Out and it has been six years in
the making, I have moments where

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:39.999
I am relieved and moments where
I cannot believe it is out.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:44.003
Is it a good thing, a bad thing?
I think I will always have these

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:48.475
this internal struggle of figuring
out if I am doing the right thing.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:53.012
And it has been validating so far
that I am doing something good.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.048
and that means the world to me.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.384
I know you have not been actively
Reading the critical reviews.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.454
And why would you, I mean how do you 
read a review of your life?

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.424
That is strange.
But the reviews are in.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.459
Right?

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:12.632
Thanks.
and rightfully so.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:16.469
This film is just brilliant.
We are going to get into it.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:20.206
I made you a promise a week ago
when we spoke that we would try

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:25.211
and have fun because I think
there is probably a desire from

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.348
people who have seen the
documentary to ask a lot of questions

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.150
about what you went through and
I can imagine that is the

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.819
reason you made that
documentary to not have to

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.922
answer those questions again and
again.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:40.560
Essentially, yeah.
But that does leads me to the

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.330
question, why did you make this
documentary, from your

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:49.068
perspective?
I think originally, I thought

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:52.605
I was going to make a
traditional tour documentary

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:56.009
about my music and about the
Revival tour.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:03:02.448
And, as I recognized my mental
state at the time I look back at

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.518
that girl and I do not even
recognize her anymore.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:11.157
It broke my heart to see myself
talking about my body and how it

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:16.996
needed to look a certain way.
I just felt really bad.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.899
I had to cancel that tour.
That was the first tour I had to

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.651
cancel.
After 55 shows you had really

00:03:23.651 --> 00:03:27.885
put the time in already.
That most people's just for the record 

00:03:27.885 --> 00:03:33.980
That's most people's full world tours, 55 shows.
We were in the middle.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:39.385
And it was really hard because I
never ever want to let anyone

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.254
down.
I always want to show up for

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.423
people.
But I knew I could not keep

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:46.459
going.
I had to stop.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.596
Then I picked it back up again
and we started to film my trip

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:54.701
to Kenya and we thought maybe we could do a
short about this adventure that

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.437
we are going on and this
experience.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:04:00.907
Then I had to go straight to
London and Paris and I quickly

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:06.713
realize that all of this stuff
that is going on in my life, it

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.949
all started with me.
How am I feeling?

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.318
how am I navigating through all of these

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.553
different things that are going on 

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:16.990
in my life how am I surviving
and

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:22.228
ultimately, it is going to be a
story about my mental health

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.832
journey, it is not going to be
necessarily a puff piece it is

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:29.569
going to show every part of me
and that's the good the bad the ugly 

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.709
and the real.

00:04:31.355 --> 00:04:36.709
I think great documentaries aren't so much reactive 
I think a lot of them can be that way

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:43.483
react on periods of life and try to retell that story 
in an entertaining way that is great to watch.

00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:50.223
But great documentary films are proactive.
And when I watch them, I feel like

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:54.127
the subject is learning about themselves.
and going on a journey.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.162
The documentary is guiding that process more 
than you are guiding the documentary.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:05:02.035
Did it feel that way, would you
have pushed forward the way that

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:04.671
you did?
I think so, I would like to

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:11.101
believe, that Alec, and I had a relationship where
even in the weakest moments when I had a lupus flareup,

00:05:11.101 --> 00:05:12.834
and it was really painful.

00:05:13.322 --> 00:05:17.183
he would ask me a few times 
if I was comfortable being recorded.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:23.556
I thought, I want to be able to
show people all of it, so just

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.859
go ahead.
That is weird to say, but it also

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:32.732
felt like a big relief because I
know I am not the only one that

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.702
is hurting that way.
It should be talked about, and

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:38.771
it should be seen.
But, what about when you saw

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:46.161
it? It’s done thing to be living it and experiencing it, 
you have this trust with the camera already in life

00:05:46.161 --> 00:05:49.916
to some degree and understand
its role but when you look

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:54.443
back at the footage, edited or otherwise
it is got to be tough for you.

00:05:54.443 --> 00:05:55.722
It’s tough for me, it’s tough for us.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:59.959
I have only actually seen it all the
way through one time.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:03.629
I, I can’t. I do not think I could 
watch it again.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:08.134
Did you watch that, basically, like almost for 
approval? Like I can let this go now?

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:14.407
I was there for parts of
editing, I could see transitions

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:18.111
and I knew how the story would
be told.

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:23.383
when it was all put together it
was really hard, it affected me for a

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:28.354
couple of days afterwards.
and I realized that was not where I

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.494
was anymore and I did not need
to revisit it.

00:06:30.494 --> 00:06:34.520
That’s a beautiful realization that as well 
to realize that you have come so far. 

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.387
I know what you mean when you feel sad
when you recognize, somebody who is yourself,  

00:06:38.387 --> 00:06:40.299
going through so much pain.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:44.604
its a reflection of the work that you
have done since then, but it

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:49.816
is kind of bittersweet. You feel for that person.  
It’s like you have a relationship with yourself.

00:06:49.816 --> 00:06:51.006
It’s kind of crazy.

00:06:51.006 --> 00:06:58.084
It is a little weird to be learning, by no means do I have life
figured out in any way shape or form

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:01.988
I just have a better
relationship with my mind.

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:05.625
None of us will, that is the
point.

00:07:05.625 --> 00:07:11.631
No.
I do, genuinely, hope to start a

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:15.935
relationship with my mind, and
my mental health that I will

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:19.639
continue to grow and I will continue 
to understand more and more.

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:22.942
Alec was the director who was behind
the camera who else did you need to forget

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.912
that was there.
There were multiple people.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:30.650
We kind of picked up and stopped
filming, people were shooting

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:35.755
other things.
There is a list of names I would

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.590
have to give you.
That is a huge amount of

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.193
trust.
It is interesting, the age of

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:48.501
seven, it is very unique, I
wonder how you recognize that

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.603
relationship between you and the
camera.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:54.319
Something that captures you.
Well, I think it’s different because

00:07:54.319 --> 00:07:55.808
I started as an actress

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:59.667
first, having a relationship
with the camera and having

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:02.643
it be invisible is just naturally

00:08:02.643 --> 00:08:05.384
part of it.
I love being on sets, I love

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:10.089
doing shows and films.
I thrive in that setting.

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:15.161
You actually want the camera to
fall in love with the character

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:21.534
you are creating. So I love that.
Then the flipside is I am walking out

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:25.838
of the hospital and there are 12
photographers screaming and wanting

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:36.282
a bad angle, a bad picture, to say 
I’m not doing well or I’m in rehab and then you’re just

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:39.051
hit with that awareness of cameras.
That can throw you off

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:44.423
completely.
It obviously became unhealthy.

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.292
I have had to had have
different relationships with how

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:50.029
it works, even in music videos
it is different than being

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:53.138
on set.
I probably prefer being on set.

00:08:53.138 --> 00:08:57.552
Of course, that is a part of why you did this 
because of that false narrative you’ve   

00:08:57.552 --> 00:09:00.000
 had to exist with throughout your life.   

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.075
This idea that you have lived
multiple lives, there is where

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:07.446
you are at any given moment and
what we see and the story they

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:12.885
choose to tell.
That is not reality, that is not

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:16.889
the narrative, this film is.
Was that a motivation for doing

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:19.091
this, did you want people to see
it once and for all?

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:25.965
Somebody asked me if I shared
so much that people are going to

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:28.434
want more, what is more?
I think I've stayed -- I think I

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:40.446
have said it all.
But I totally appreciated that

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:43.983
question.
It is The ending of this movie,

00:09:43.983 --> 00:09:50.656
is me right here and now.
I want to talk about tools

00:09:50.656 --> 00:10:00.199
and where it began, for you to
work on yourself.

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:03.069
There is an interesting scene in
the film where you described

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:07.106
being terrified of thunderstorms
as a kid.

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:09.842
When I first got out, I did
not know how I would cope with

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:14.580
my diagnosis.
What if it happened again?

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:18.050
What if next time, I did not
come back.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.587
I needed to keep learning about
it, I needed to take it day by

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:25.658
day.
When I was a kid, I was

00:10:25.658 --> 00:10:30.529
terrified of thunderstorms.
I grew up in Texas and I was so

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:33.032
scared that lightning and
thunder would mean a tornado is

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:37.737
coming.
But I learned that storms mean

00:10:37.737 --> 00:10:42.408
lightning and thunder and the
more I learned about it the less

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:46.570
afraid I would be it really
helped.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:50.049
[applause]
That feels like, to me, the

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:54.987
beginning of self-help.
Would you trace it back to that?

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:57.923
Yes.
I 1000% would have to give my

00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:02.061
mom credit for that.
I felt so scared of so many

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:08.034
things in life, because I
felt anxious, that I needed to

00:11:08.034 --> 00:11:14.106
be the best that I could be.
My mom was the person who

00:11:14.106 --> 00:11:18.244
allowed me to be the person I
wanted to be, did not judge me,

00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:23.049
and loved me through it 
and would give me the information and tools for me

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:27.219
to grow.
Instead of instilling more fear

00:11:27.219 --> 00:11:33.926
in me she educated me on the
things I was terrified of, and

00:11:33.926 --> 00:11:37.302
she would give me that strength.
That is interesting, it is

00:11:37.302 --> 00:11:42.942
how you apply it to your life,
and how it works for you.

00:11:42.942 --> 00:11:44.177
What works for you?

00:11:44.177 --> 00:11:48.000
You know I love yoga, there’s certain things 
I know that if I don’t do them…

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:53.205
I’m not good at yoga.  That’s for damn sure.
I didn’t say I was good at it, but it

00:11:53.205 --> 00:11:56.381
definitely works for me. What works for you?

00:11:56.381 --> 00:12:01.420
It is the little things, I
just had COVID, I thought, here

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:06.259
it comes. I was gonna get a little
depressed and go down a spiral.

00:12:06.259 --> 00:12:07.259
I immediately recognize the

00:12:07.259 --> 00:12:10.930
little things that I needed to
do to get out of it.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:15.801
I decided to change the things
that I was watching to things

00:12:15.801 --> 00:12:19.872
that were well-written and
beautiful and happy, I changed

00:12:19.872 --> 00:12:23.642
the music I was listening to, I
wanted to listen to positive

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:30.983
things and be inspired.
It's something like taking a walk, calling a

00:12:30.983 --> 00:12:37.156
therapist, calling a sponsor,
all of these things that seem so

00:12:37.156 --> 00:12:44.396
minuscule, that you do not think
will work or matter, getting up

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:49.935
and looking at yourself and
being OK with who the person is

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:52.304
on the others.
I love that you mentioned

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:56.542
music, what is on your positive
playlist?

00:12:56.542 --> 00:13:00.146
Oh my God, The new album from
Taylor Swift right now.

00:13:00.146 --> 00:13:06.118
All of it.
Flawless.

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:10.890
A remarkable body of work.
Do you allow music to keep you

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.958
company when you are sad?
1000%.

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:20.366
Essentially, I was raised in a
world where our emotions were

00:13:20.366 --> 00:13:24.837
illustrated by music.
My mom grew up listening to

00:13:24.837 --> 00:13:30.376
Patsy Cline, and Joni Mitchell,
and Janis Joplin.

00:13:30.376 --> 00:13:36.081
My dad grew up listening to
Other music, like Selena Quintanilla.

00:13:36.081 --> 00:13:40.686
Who was named after.
He had a flair for R&amp;B.

00:13:40.686 --> 00:13:50.229
I was inundated with so many
styles of music.

00:13:50.229 --> 00:13:55.267
It was a part of my life.
I was 11 years old listening to

00:13:55.267 --> 00:13:58.537
Coldplay or Maroon 5 and
pretending that I was in love

00:13:58.537 --> 00:14:02.007
and I was in a breakup in the car.
I would pretend that I felt

00:14:02.007 --> 00:14:05.377
these emotions.
You are not pretending, that

00:14:05.377 --> 00:14:11.617
is the beauty of it.
I was pretend crying.

00:14:11.617 --> 00:14:15.988
When you feel that so vividly
as a kid, and we all feel that

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:19.758
when we love something.
We feel it.

00:14:19.758 --> 00:14:25.531
And then If you stay feeling
that, whenever, 10 or 12 years

00:14:25.531 --> 00:14:30.769
later, you find yourself doing
what, singing a song with Chris

00:14:30.769 --> 00:14:33.272
Martin.
[LAUGHTER]

00:14:33.272 --> 00:14:36.775
I did not actually put that
together.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:41.113
You only get there if you
feel it, there is no pretending.

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:44.049
That is true.
There are incredibly poignant

00:14:44.049 --> 00:14:47.820
moments when you come home.
We have seen this before.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:51.523
We all go home.
It is great.

00:14:51.523 --> 00:14:58.664
You were not just going home to
reflect on the experience you

00:14:58.664 --> 00:15:01.734
were searching for purpose
there.

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:04.536
What was it like, you were
visiting friends and neighbors.

00:15:04.536 --> 00:15:11.944
You catch up with somebody who
went to school with you and it

00:15:11.944 --> 00:15:14.113
feels so full circle, it is
crazy.

00:15:14.113 --> 00:15:18.817
do you know who this is?
It is Selena Gomez.

00:15:18.817 --> 00:15:20.019
My name is Selena.
[laughter]

00:15:20.019 --> 00:15:23.022
The one that you hear the songs
of, yeah.

00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:35.334
[screaming]
She is my dramatic one.

00:15:35.334 --> 00:15:44.977
That is OK.
Yes, she is real, she grew up

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:48.847
down the street from me.
Mommy went to school with her.

00:15:48.847 --> 00:15:54.787
Can I have a hug?
Does that make you happy?

00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:59.558
Yeah.
Thank you, I appreciate it.

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:01.827
It is good to see you.
I am glad that everything is

00:16:01.827 --> 00:16:05.864
good for you, to see you go
through all of that was

00:16:05.864 --> 00:16:11.870
inspiring.
Thank you.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:19.011
I feel better.
We love you.

00:16:19.011 --> 00:16:22.982
[applause]
every time I go home I

00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:25.217
Usually drive by my old
neighborhood, just because it

00:16:25.217 --> 00:16:30.222
feels so good.
It reminds me.

00:16:30.222 --> 00:16:33.492
Every time I am home I usually
love going to visit people.

00:16:33.492 --> 00:16:46.972
At that time, I invaded peoples
personal space.

00:16:46.972 --> 00:16:53.545
I could be disrupting neighbors,
or with my friends, watching her

00:16:53.545 --> 00:16:58.150
have children and a totally different life.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:04.957
Thinking I could have that life,
I am nowhere near that.

00:17:04.957 --> 00:17:11.764
It is not a bad thing.
You gave her daughter this

00:17:11.764 --> 00:17:19.638
moment, and she gave you genuine
love and concern from someone

00:17:19.638 --> 00:17:24.209
you knew long ago.
It was such a lovely human moment.

00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:31.450
It was the trade gone right.
When she said she was happy I

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:41.026
was doing well, she means that,
it doesn't matter I've become

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:43.462
whatever.
I am still Selena.

00:17:43.462 --> 00:17:48.600
We see a strife for a
different type of purpose.

00:17:48.600 --> 00:18:00.453
You found purpose as a young child, 
and it was successful

00:18:00.453 --> 00:18:10.656
when during the making of the documentary, did you
realize, you were getting to a

00:18:10.656 --> 00:18:15.894
new purpose in life?
Getting beyond fame and reaching

00:18:15.894 --> 00:18:21.800
for something more substantial?
Perhaps, it was when I was

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:25.704
having downs and I could not
hide them.

00:18:25.704 --> 00:18:31.176
Whether the camera was there or
not, I could not get out of my

00:18:31.176 --> 00:18:35.047
own head.
I realized those moments would

00:18:35.047 --> 00:18:41.380
stop me from creating a great
tour, a good year or a good attitude.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.056
It was affecting me.

00:18:44.056 --> 00:18:54.633
I knew we were capturing these
moments, this is real, this is

00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:58.770
what people are walking
through, this is bigger than

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:04.977
what we are worried about.
There were multiple moments,

00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:08.567
where I thought it would be bigger
than just me.

00:19:08.567 --> 00:19:14.900
It begins a really fascinating journey in life when you 
realize that you want to go and alter your purpose.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:18.290
People around you might not

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:20.225
understand what that means.

00:19:20.225 --> 00:19:26.698
There is a promo cycle, to be
fair, they happen all of the

00:19:26.698 --> 00:19:34.996
time, but you are ready to
announce this even in a small way.

00:19:34.996 --> 00:19:36.646
You want to do something bigger,

00:19:36.646 --> 00:19:40.345
and it doesn't land.
I looked at your face and it

00:19:40.345 --> 00:19:47.719
does not land, I looked at your
face.

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:51.156
This will take a long time.
Exactly.

00:19:51.156 --> 00:20:03.135
We celebrate you for the work
that you have been doing.

00:20:03.135 --> 00:20:06.605
These mean something to you now.
Can you talk how talk about

00:20:06.605 --> 00:20:09.608
how fulfilling it has been to be
in this space?

00:20:09.608 --> 00:20:15.714
It feels wonderful.
It started when I was 14 and I

00:20:15.714 --> 00:20:23.355
had a single mother come up to
me, they were from Mexico in a

00:20:23.355 --> 00:20:27.593
town close to where my family is
from.

00:20:27.593 --> 00:20:32.764
She said thank you for being who
you are, they can -- my children

00:20:32.764 --> 00:20:38.670
can look at someone on TV who
looks like them.

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:43.642
I did not understand it because
I am who I am.

00:20:43.642 --> 00:20:46.378
Then I recognized the
responsibility that I have been

00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:52.751
given with my platform, I truly
felt it was bigger than me.

00:20:52.751 --> 00:20:59.424
When I had dark moments I would
get back up over and over again,

00:20:59.424 --> 00:21:08.600
it was hard to get up, but if I
stood in a fit of pain, I would

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:12.971
be letting you all down.
I could not live with that.

00:21:12.971 --> 00:21:16.475
I could not do that.
I had to learn how to do that

00:21:16.475 --> 00:21:20.746
myself.
I had to tell people, I cannot

00:21:20.746 --> 00:21:29.855
do that right now.
Now I can be the best version of

00:21:29.855 --> 00:21:38.430
myself for other people.
You help others do for

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:42.367
themselves.
That is what I'm take -- that is

00:21:42.367 --> 00:21:45.337
what I am taking from the next
chapter of your life.

00:21:45.337 --> 00:21:54.579
It ends with you making a
commitment to this conversation.

00:21:54.579 --> 00:22:00.185
When we met for the first time,
I recognize that you were really

00:22:00.185 --> 00:22:06.091
in this documentary.
I felt that and I believe it's

00:22:06.091 --> 00:22:10.262
reflected in the conversation we had.

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:13.899
We landed on a subject we are
both passionate about,

00:22:13.899 --> 00:22:21.073
increasing awareness around
mental health, and self-help.

00:22:21.073 --> 00:22:25.210
We are seeing changes and you
have been instrumental to making

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:27.079
changes happen.
I want to give you a round of

00:22:27.079 --> 00:22:28.313
applause for that.
[applause]

00:22:28.313 --> 00:22:33.719
Thank you so much.
I appreciate it.

00:22:33.719 --> 00:22:38.590
you have started to do the groundwork.

00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:42.394
How has your experience been,
are we going in the right

00:22:42.394 --> 00:22:45.630
direction, where are we going?
Do you feel like it's working?

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:56.541
 I want to say yes.
I don't mind being a person who

00:22:56.541 --> 00:23:02.781
is the voice of mental health,
it is who I am, it is my life, I

00:23:02.781 --> 00:23:06.651
want people to become more
comfortable with that

00:23:06.651 --> 00:23:13.091
conversation and I want it to
stop being a label that

00:23:13.091 --> 00:23:16.728
terrifies people more for people
to stop thinking it is not a

00:23:16.728 --> 00:23:19.998
real thing.
If I released this documentary

00:23:19.998 --> 00:23:32.611
before the pandemic, they may
have thought I was crazy.

00:23:32.611 --> 00:23:38.116
It was interesting to hear,
people react to this movie and

00:23:38.116 --> 00:23:42.521
actually say, I did not know I
had that, I struggle with that

00:23:42.521 --> 00:23:49.728
as well.
It's no surprise that one of

00:23:49.728 --> 00:23:58.437
it is no surprise that one of
your most genuine songs is your most popular.

00:23:58.437 --> 00:24:01.840
Now that you understand your

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:06.344
truth better than ever, and have the courage to share it.
We are waiting for the album of your career.

00:24:06.344 --> 00:24:08.780
[LAUGHTER]

00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:16.655
[APPLAUSE]
No pressure.

00:24:16.655 --> 00:24:22.894
You set the bar, not me.
I'm just acknowledging it.

00:24:22.894 --> 00:24:25.597
If I am being completely
honest, which I have been.

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:38.677
It has been really difficult.
I am used to just making music.

00:24:38.677 --> 00:24:54.793
Now I am telling stories about
people, experiences, now I have

00:24:54.793 --> 00:24:58.630
to tell these stories and people
will ask a lot of questions.

00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:05.570
They will be happy to get
another album.

00:25:05.570 --> 00:25:08.840
You didn't have -- you did not
have a choice before.

00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:15.213
Everyone decided these were the
stories you needed to tell.

00:25:15.213 --> 00:25:18.884
Every artist on the planet gets
To decide how they talk about

00:25:18.884 --> 00:25:25.924
The relationship.
You have just caught up to every

00:25:25.924 --> 00:25:29.327
artist on the planet.
Thank God.

00:25:29.327 --> 00:25:35.667
I feel accomplished.
you can do it your way.

00:25:35.667 --> 00:25:38.803
I have earned it.
I do not want to release

00:25:38.803 --> 00:25:44.476
anything that is not perfect, it
is getting there.

00:25:44.476 --> 00:25:52.050
We are getting to fan questions.
My favorite.

00:25:52.050 --> 00:26:00.091
If I could end the rest of my
life asking fan questions.

00:26:00.091 --> 00:26:09.267
how does it feel to be your
True and vulnerable self?

00:26:09.267 --> 00:26:16.007
I feel like I can relax now.
Now you know everything I was

00:26:16.007 --> 00:26:20.245
walking through, you did not
judge me, you were there for me

00:26:20.245 --> 00:26:23.748
constantly.
It made me feel normal.

00:26:23.748 --> 00:26:30.188
I appreciate that.
What scene in this film are you

00:26:30.188 --> 00:26:33.959
most proud of?
Probably when I was

00:26:33.959 --> 00:26:39.965
rehearsing for the AMAs  I was
not ready.

00:26:39.965 --> 00:26:49.541
I started to listen to a song.
I felt like that was me really

00:26:49.541 --> 00:26:55.447
Trying to push through something
That was difficult.

00:26:55.447 --> 00:27:02.320
That moment meant more to me.
That was me trying to heal.

00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:13.031
It is terrifying to get up and
sing.

00:27:13.031 --> 00:27:14.866
It was such a personal
release?

00:27:14.866 --> 00:27:21.239
It was, it was such a gift.
Go and look at any

00:27:21.239 --> 00:27:27.979
documentary film, the -- there
is not a scene in which Selena

00:27:27.979 --> 00:27:36.888
misses a note.
It was great to see you do that.

00:27:36.888 --> 00:27:42.427
What was the hardest thing for
You?

00:27:42.427 --> 00:27:49.968
probably the tour.
It was really honest.

00:27:49.968 --> 00:27:57.475
I had been so inundated with
comments about my body.

00:27:57.475 --> 00:28:01.112
There was a reason I was talking
about myself, that way.

00:28:01.112 --> 00:28:07.085
I did not make that up.
I had been told that I needed to

00:28:07.085 --> 00:28:14.159
look better, dress cooler, my
tour was kinda lame, I was trying to

00:28:14.159 --> 00:28:18.730
be someone I was not, that was
happening all of the time, to

00:28:18.730 --> 00:28:25.603
me.
I think that is abusive.

00:28:25.603 --> 00:28:32.343
I am never going to let anyone
make me feel that way.

00:28:32.343 --> 00:28:39.617
I gained my strength back when I
realized, that girl wasn't lame,

00:28:39.617 --> 00:28:45.557
was not lame, she did not
need a better body, I am exactly

00:28:45.557 --> 00:28:50.395
who I am.
When I was released from the

00:28:50.395 --> 00:28:57.769
voice in my life, I did not
fall, I rose up.

00:28:57.769 --> 00:29:03.708
That's -- that is the best part.
[applause]

00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:09.614
Thank you.
I know there was a longer edit.

00:29:09.614 --> 00:29:11.683
for sure.

00:29:11.683 --> 00:29:16.087
[LAUGHTER]
that is not even insider

00:29:16.087 --> 00:29:20.425
talk, every film has a longer
edit.

00:29:20.425 --> 00:29:32.170
Was there anything you wish you
could have gotten in there?

00:29:32.170 --> 00:29:36.174
probably more content with my
Fans.

00:29:36.174 --> 00:29:39.677
Because the pandemic happened, I
Canceled my tour.

00:29:39.677 --> 00:29:42.213
The meet and greets were my only
connection to people.

00:29:42.213 --> 00:29:46.017
Me being here is such a high.
I have missed this more than

00:29:46.017 --> 00:29:50.188
Anything.
I can wait to meet all of you

00:29:50.188 --> 00:29:54.926
and hug you.
Not to put too fine a point

00:29:54.926 --> 00:29:58.763
on it, is this the first time in
a long time that you have had

00:29:58.763 --> 00:30:01.466
this experience?
Yes, basically.

00:30:01.466 --> 00:30:05.470
I am so happy.
It feels good.

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:13.426
How does it feel to know that 
you're changing our lives?

00:30:13.426 --> 00:30:17.554
and making us feel seen when it 
comes to mental health

00:30:17.554 --> 00:30:29.994
and this question ends with I love you
I love all of you.

00:30:29.994 --> 00:30:48.346
If I am able to help one person
with this, I am on cloud nine.

00:30:48.346 --> 00:30:52.016
I hope I am remembered by my
heart.

00:30:52.016 --> 00:30:59.157
Simply wanting to see people for
who they are and love them

00:30:59.157 --> 00:31:02.427
truly, authentically, and does
purely as possibly I can.

00:31:02.427 --> 00:31:09.467
[applause]
In this beautiful Apple Tower

00:31:09.467 --> 00:31:14.606
Theatre in downtown Los Angeles,
I want to honor the fact that

00:31:14.606 --> 00:31:20.245
you get to see your fans for the
first time in a very long time.

00:31:20.245 --> 00:31:22.947
We just came out of the crazy few years.

00:31:22.947 --> 00:31:25.083
This would not have been
Possible.

00:31:25.083 --> 00:31:30.455
What you went through made it
Seem further away.

00:31:30.455 --> 00:31:35.627
I wanted to give you a chance to
Talk to your fans directly And

00:31:35.627 --> 00:31:38.863
say something to them.
And we can and like that.

00:31:38.863 --> 00:31:43.801
I will end up talking your ear off when I meet you.

00:31:43.801 --> 00:31:50.742
Because I like that.
Me releasing this was one of the

00:31:50.742 --> 00:31:54.112
most terrifying things that I
have done.

00:31:54.112 --> 00:31:58.883
I am so grateful that people
like you are able to watch it,

00:31:58.883 --> 00:32:04.489
if a friend is walking through
something, that you are able to

00:32:04.489 --> 00:32:14.098
be a voice for them.
I know it is such a cliché, and at

00:32:14.098 --> 00:32:16.301
the end of the day it is just me,

00:32:16.301 --> 00:32:22.941
my core friends, and us.
I want to continue to be the

00:32:22.941 --> 00:32:27.445
best version of myself that I
can and to love you guys fully

00:32:27.445 --> 00:32:29.881
and truly for who you are
because you do that for me.

00:32:29.881 --> 00:32:32.618
Thank you, so much.
[applause]

00:32:32.618 --> 00:32:39.990
♪♪

